{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784147432,"nonce":"TPFVpUbyL5yqCWXHJ7+pc3I5J/0=","title":"Expose the **catalog** and **parameter interface** so a client can discover manually-dispatchable pipelines at a ref and read their param schema before dispatching — the API the UI (slice 4) and CLI both eat (invariant #5: one validator, no private backchannel).","message":"Scope, end-to-end:\n- **Catalog** — `GET /v1/repos/:id/pipelines?ref=` returns a lightweight list: pipeline name, whether it is `manual`-dispatchable, and the resolved commit SHA for that ref. No full compile just to list.\n- **Interface (describe)** — `GET /v1/repos/:id/pipelines/:name/interface?ref=` compiles the selected pipeline and returns its typed parameter specs (`name, type, required, default?, options?, validate?, description?`) plus the resolved SHA. Two-call design: compile-for-interface only happens on selection.\n- **Ref → SHA** — describe resolves the ref to a concrete SHA and returns it, so the UI can dispatch that exact SHA (slice 2) with no form/run skew.\n- **OpenAPI** — both endpoints documented; the generated client picks them up.\n- **CLI** — `scarab run \u003crepo\u003e \u003cpipeline\u003e --ref \u003cref\u003e --param k=v …` uses describe + dispatch; strings from `--param` flow through the same `coerce` path.\n\n\n- [ ] `GET …/pipelines?ref=` lists pipelines at the ref with a `manual?` flag and resolved SHA; a repo with no `.scarab/` returns an empty list, not an error.\n- [ ] `GET …/pipelines/:name/interface?ref=` returns the compiled typed param specs + SHA; a compile error surfaces as a structured diagnostic.\n- [ ] Both endpoints are ref-scoped and appear in OpenAPI; the generated client exposes them.\n- [ ] `scarab run … --param k=v` dispatches via describe+dispatch; a bad param value fails with the same structured per-param error the API returns.\n- [ ] The interface response is a pure function of the compiled IR (same validator as dispatch) — no duplicated parsing logic.\n\n\n- 0a3b098 (slice 2)","files":null}]}